# Pressable: size only — chrome on inner View

On a `Pressable`, **only size / layout-for-hit-area styles** are allowed:
- `width`, `height`, `minWidth`, `minHeight`, `maxWidth`, `maxHeight`
- `flex`, `flexGrow`, `flexShrink`, `flexBasis`, `alignSelf`
- Optional pressed feedback: `opacity`
- `hitSlop`

**Everything else** must live on an **inner `View`**:
- `backgroundColor`
- borders (`borderWidth`, `borderColor`, `borderRadius`, …)
- shadows / elevation
- **padding** (all variants)
- margin, gap, alignItems, justifyContent, overflow, etc.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Pressable
  onPress={onPress}
  style={{
    backgroundColor: colors.orbit,
    borderRadius: 12,
    padding: 16,
    width: '100%',
  }}
>
  <Text>Action</Text>
</Pressable>

// ✅ GOOD
<Pressable
  onPress={onPress}
  style={({ pressed }) => [{ width: '100%' }, { opacity: pressed ? 0.9 : 1 }]}
>
  <View
    style={{
      backgroundColor: colors.orbit,
      borderRadius: 12,
      padding: 16,
      alignItems: 'center',
      justifyContent: 'center',
    }}
  >
    <Text>Action</Text>
  </View>
</Pressable>
```

Never put visual chrome or padding on `Pressable`. Size on Pressable; the rest on View.
